      ],
      "type": "paragraph",
      "reading_order": 6,
      "text": "The two most commonly used attention functions are additive attention [2], and dot-product (multiplicative) attention. Dot-product attention is identical to our algorithm, except for the scaling factor of √1 $\\frac { 1 } { \\sqrt { d _ { k } } }$ . Additive attention computes the compatibility function using a feed-forward network with a single hidden layer. While the two are similar in theoretical complexity, dot-product attention is much faster and more space-efficient in practice, since it can be implemented using highly optimized matrix multiplication code. ",
      "source": "mineru",
      "quality": "structured_review_required",
      "metadata": {
        "mineru_type": "text",
        "text_level": null,
        "reconstruction": "MinerU structured output; verify against original region",
